WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.336
-Thank you. Thank you.
Thank you for that...

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.604
for that wonderful welcome.

00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:08.574
That applause actually lasted
longer than Anthony Scaramucci.

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:10.076
Absolutely...

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:13.913
Welcome.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.681
I'm your host,
Jimmy Fallon, everybody.

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:17.516
Well, people are still talking
about Anthony Scaramucci

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:20.352
getting fired.
He lasted just six days,

00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:21.787
making him the shortest-serving

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:23.956
White House Communications
Director ever.

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:25.458
But don't feel bad.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.226
Publishers have offered him
a lot of money

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:29.195
to write a tell-all pamphlet
about the experience.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.563
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.698
Three pages.

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:33.967
[ Laughs ]

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.935
Three pages,
double-spaced, yeah.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.970
-24-point font.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.772
-He only lasted six days.

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:42.041
I mean, there were
White House fence jumpers

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.476
who lasted longer than that.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:45.178
-Come on!
-Six days is nothing.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.614
-Ohh!

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.482
-But get this.
Trump is apparently looking

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.617
for a less prominent position
for Scaramucci

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:55.655
that wouldn't require him
to be seen very often.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.589
Scaramucci said,
"You want me to be First Lady?"

00:00:57.589 --> 00:00:59.692
And you go, "No, no,
that's not what I mean by that.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.894
Where's Melania? Melania!

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:04.697
She's just -- She's late.
She's arriving late."

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.066
But it's been a rough week
for Scaramucci.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.402
In fact, I saw that in
the latest alumni directory

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:12.805
for Harvard Law School, he was
mistakenly listed as dead.

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:14.740
It's nothing personal.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.475
That's just what happens
in Harvard

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:18.110
if you don't donate any money.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:21.981
Yeah. They get...

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:25.017
But Anthony Scaramucci joined
a long list of officials

00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:26.752
that President Trump has fired.

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:28.621
That might explain
this commercial that I just saw.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.789
Watch this.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.691
-Are you looking for work?
-Yes.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.892
-Unsure about your future?
-Yes.

00:01:33.892 --> 00:01:35.361
-Or maybe you have a job,

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.297
but you're worried you could be
let go at any moment?

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.665
-Absolutely.

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:41.734 line:0%
-Then forget about LinkedIn
and join KickedOut,

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.936 line:0%
the only jobs website
made for people

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:46.239 line:0%
who've been fired from
the Trump administration.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.274 line:0%
-Fantastic.
-KickedOut knows exactly

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.576 line:0%
how to get you
that amazing new job.

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:52.077 line:0%
We take your résumé

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:54.814 line:0%
and delete anything that says
you've worked for Donald Trump.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.983 line:0%
-Isn't that wonderful?
-KickedOut.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:02:00.286 line:0%
Sorry. We can't help you get on
"Dancing with the Stars."

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.054
-KickedOut.
-KickedOut.

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:04.791
-KickedOut is the new LinkedIn.
-It's called KickedOut.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.225
[ Applause ]

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:08.060
-Actually, earlier today,

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.295
the White House announced
Scaramucci's replacement,

00:02:10.295 --> 00:02:13.333
and we have him right now
via satellite from Washington.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:16.068
Please welcome Donald Trump's
new communications director,

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:17.236
Andrew Moore.

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:18.738 line:0%
Thank you
for being here, Andrew.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:22.074 line:0%
-Thank you.
Thank you, Jimmy.

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:23.342 line:0%
I'm excited for the challenges

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:24.877 line:0%
of being
communications director,

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:26.779 line:0%
and I'm confident
that I'll be fully capable

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.682 line:0%
of seamlessly transitioning
into the new role.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:32.018
-Now, Andrew,
what experience do you have

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.586
that qualifies you to take on

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.654
this very important role
in the White House?

00:02:35.654 --> 00:02:37.222
-That's a good question, Jimmy.

00:02:37.222 --> 00:02:39.625
For the past eight years,
I've been fighting for the --

00:02:39.625 --> 00:02:40.659
-Wait. I'm so -- I'm so sorry.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:41.961
I'm not sure
what's going on here.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.730
What -- What happened to Andrew?

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.131
-Oh, he was fired.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.766
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.569
-Just now?
-Yep. Check Trump's twitter.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:51.804
Anyway, I'm taking over the job.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.107
-Oh.
Well, who -- who are you?

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.275 line:0%
-My name is Jerome Kennard.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:57.443 line:0%
-All right, well, Mr. Kennard,

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.811 line:0%
I'm not quite sure
where to begin,

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.213
but are you nervous
about taking over

00:03:01.213 --> 00:03:03.115
the communications director
position?

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:06.386
-A little nervous, yeah.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:07.720
-Wait.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.522
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.990
W-Who are<i> you?</i>

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.025 line:0%
-I'm the new White House
communications director,

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:14.526 line:0%
Bob Wellington.

00:03:14.526 --> 00:03:16.996 line:0%
Uh, Jerome was fired.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:19.531 line:0%
<i> -You're</i> the new White House
communications director?

00:03:19.531 --> 00:03:22.067 line:0%
-That's right, Jimmy.
Matt Grady. Nice to meet you.

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:23.269 line:0%
-Now, this -- Wait.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.871 line:0%
Another -- Another new
communications director?

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.773
That's the fourth
new communications director

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:28.374
in one minute.
How is that possible?

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.609
-Heh. I know.
It's a little crazy.

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:33.679
-Wait. You again? Andrew?
They -- They rehired you?

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:36.282
-Oh, no.
I just left my mug here.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:39.685
It was the only thing
I had enough time to
put on my desk, so...

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:42.354
-Well, then, who<i> is</i>
the new communications director

00:03:42.354 --> 00:03:43.589
at the White House?

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:47.093 line:0%
-It's me, Jimmy.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.829 line:0%
I'll just do it myself.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:54.000 line:0%
-Donald Trump, you're your own
new communications director?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.868
-Yes. Oh.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.169
No, I guess not anymore.

00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:59.738
I'm looking at my Twitter
account. I just fired me.

00:03:59.738 --> 00:04:01.440
-All right. That's enough.
Thank you very much.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.276
Andrew Moore, Jerome Kennard,
Bob Wellington,

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.911
Matt Grady, and Donald Trump,
everyone.

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:08.948
Confusing. Confusing.

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:11.416
Well, yesterday was White House
chief of staff John Kelly's

00:04:11.416 --> 00:04:13.218
first day on the job.

00:04:13.218 --> 00:04:15.154
But it got awkward
when he showed up and said,

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:17.490
"Why are you writing my name on
the door in dry-erase marker?"

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.391
Wait. That's not a good sign.

00:04:19.391 --> 00:04:20.693
-That's not good.
-No.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:23.629
-But it's crazy.
As of today, 12 top government

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:26.265
or White House officials
have been fired or resigned

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:28.134
since Trump took office.
Yeah.

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:30.836
And Trump was like,
"Just five more eliminations

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:32.371
until I announce the winner."

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:34.340
That's not how this works!

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.910
It's not a reality show.
What are you doing?

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.078
The other big story
that people are talking about

00:04:40.078 --> 00:04:42.614
is that Trump dictated
Don Jr.'s misleading statement

00:04:42.614 --> 00:04:44.984
about meeting with
a Russian lawyer last year,

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:47.520
which puts the president
in legal jeopardy.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.822
When Trump heard
that he was in jeopardy,

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:51.457
he said,
"I'd rather play Family Feud.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:53.325
Show me collusion!"

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:56.228
Ber!

00:04:56.228 --> 00:04:57.763
Here's a local story.

00:04:57.763 --> 00:04:59.665
Utility workers
here in New York City

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:02.935
retrieved a woman's wedding ring
that she dropped down a sewer...

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.337
while the rat handing it back

00:05:05.337 --> 00:05:07.640
was like, "Always a bridesmaid.
[Inhales sharply]

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.009
Congratulations."

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:12.144
[ Applause ]

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:14.680
Well, last night, was
the "Men Tell All" episode

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.115
of "The Bachelorette,"

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.250
where the guys who were
eliminated from the show

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.986
talked about their experiences.

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:21.554
The fans love it,
and I think it might have

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.890
inspired another show, too.
Check this out.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:28.093
-Tonight on ABC, tune in
for a very special event,

00:05:28.093 --> 00:05:30.463
"The White House Men Tell All."

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:33.433 line:0%
Watch Reince talk about having
his heart broken by Donald.

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:36.302 line:0%
-Well, it's disappointing, but
I don't think it's over yet.

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:40.005 line:0%
-See Sean try to find the words
to describe saying goodbye.

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:41.674 line:0%
-I think -- Let's -- Let's --

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:43.709 line:0%
I think at some point,
you know, he's -- he's --

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:47.680 line:0%
-And Anthony reveals the very
last thing he said to Donald.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.082 line:0%
-[Bleep] Thank you.

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:53.619 line:0%
-That's all tonight on
"The White House Men Tell All."

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:56.989
-"The White House Men Tell All."

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:59.625
And finally,
this is going viral.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.360
The other day
on a Southwest flight,

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.462
a little boy greeted everyone
with a fist bump

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:05.097
on his way to his seat.

00:06:05.097 --> 00:06:06.999
It's pretty cute.
Check this out.

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:08.401
-He wants to fist-bump you.

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:10.369
-Let's do it.
[ Imitates explosion ]

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:13.305
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.305 --> 00:06:15.307
-Yeah. And this is nice.

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:17.543
It only delayed the flight
for two hours.

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:19.445
[ Applause ]

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:21.848
"Get your kid in the seat!"

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:23.115
He was so good at using his fist

00:06:23.115 --> 00:06:24.617
that he was just hired
by United Airlines.

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:26.719
There you go, guys.
We have a great show tonight.

